 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The session is a cookie that holds the member and the session's expiry, signed with the shared session key
+`LARDER_SESSION_KEY`. Any web server checks the cookie with that key, so a member stays logged in whichever server
+answers and across deploys. A forged or expired cookie logs no one in
+([keep sessions in signed cookies](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-signed-cookies.md)).
+
+## Known limits
+
+- The server cannot end one member's session before it expires. The session still ends after 30 minutes without a
+  request. Rotating the session key ends every member's session at once, so the key is rotated only between pickups.
 
